################################################################################
 THREAT: Service failure -> root-cause detection (fault management)
################################################################################
 Description   : A dependency (storage) fails; every service that uses it starts failing too, producing many unrelated-looking alarms.
 Why relevant  : Storage is the single writer of all readings; when it fails ingestion and analytics both return errors and operators see alarms from several locations at once.
 Exploitation  : Crash, resource exhaustion (e.g. after a DoS), or an attacker stopping the service.
 Monitoring    : Prometheus: up, analytics_storage_errors_total, ingestion_readings_total{result=storage_error}, registry_instances. Wazuh: rule 100201 (HTTP 5xx) per agent with its hierarchical ID.
 Action-resp.  : Correlation rule SSLERootCauseStorageDown names storage as the cause; the registry stops handing out the dead instance; recovery is checked when storage comes back.
################################################################################

